IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `saa-student`

-- Student Assistance Regulations 2021 -- the events prescribed for s 48 of the Student Assistance Act 1973 (what an ABSTUDY
-- recipient must report within 14 days), read from the deposited Regulations instead of asked as a fact. A module beside
-- saa-student.l4; it works out that module's `it is a prescribed event` input and calls its `Must I tell the Department of the
-- event`, restating none of its rules.
--
-- SEAT: the ABSTUDY student (or the parent who receives ABSTUDY for the student), as in saa-student.l4. "Something has
-- changed. Is it one of the things I must report, and by when?"
--
-- Edition: Compilation No. 1, compilation date 6 April 2022, includes amendments up to F2022L00524 (register id F2022C00508),
-- deposited at ../../../student-assistance-regulations-2021/registers/source-bundle/F2021L00201.txt (retrieved 2026-10-23).
--
-- IN: Part 3 Division 2 (the ABSTUDY Scheme: regs 12-21) and reg 29 (notify Services Australia). OUT: Division 3 (the
-- Assistance for Isolated Children Scheme, regs 22-28), Part 4 (transitional). The Minister's determinations under ss 38A(2)
-- and 41D(2): none was found in force on the Federal Register (searched 23 October 2026 by title, "Student Assistance" and
-- "ABSTUDY"); NOTES.md finding 13 says what follows and what does not.

§ `Student Assistance Regulations 2021 -- what I must report on ABSTUDY`

§§ `regs 12 to 21 -- the prescribed events`

DECLARE `Who receives the ABSTUDY` IS ONE OF
    `I am the student, with independent status`
    `I am the student, with dependent status`
    `I am a parent of the student, receiving it for the student`

DECLARE `What changed` IS ONE OF
    -- reg 13(1) (courses)
    `the student did not enrol before the enrolment period ended`
    `the student enrolled but did not start within 3 weeks of the course first being offered`
    `the student's enrolment was cancelled`
    `the student stopped taking part in the course without cancelling enrolment`
    `a school student stopped studying full-time as the school requires`
    `the circumstances behind a 25% or 66% concessional study load changed`
    `a tertiary or secondary non-school student's study load fell below three-quarters of full-time`
    -- reg 14 (personal relationships)
    `someone became or stopped being the student's partner`
    `a dependent child of the student will be outside Australia`
    `someone stopped being a dependent child of the student`
    `someone became a parent of the student`
    `someone other than the student stopped being a dependent child of the student's parent`
    -- reg 16 (residence)
    `the student changed place of residence or permanent home`
    `the student, on rent assistance, started living with someone or in government housing for which rent is payable`
    `the student, on remote area allowance, will be away from the permanent home for more than 8 weeks`
    `the student will be outside Australia`
    -- reg 17 (benefits)
    `another education or training benefit, a veterans' payment, Living Away from Home Allowance or a compensation payment became payable for the student`
    `the student's Pensioner Education Supplement qualifying payment stopped`
    `the student became, or stopped being, a new apprentice`
    -- regs 18-20 (income and assets)
    `the student's or partner's income for a reporting period was more than the estimate given`
    `a parent's income for the year exceeded, or will exceed, the estimate by 25% or more`
    `the student's (or the student and partner's) assets exceed the personal assets test limit`
    -- reg 21 (other)
    `the student stopped being an Australian citizen`
    `the student stopped being recognised as an Indigenous person`
    `the student stopped working in a job`
    `the student was taken into lawful custody`
    `the student died`
    `something else`

-- reg 14(1): "if the ABSTUDY payee is the student and the student has independent status": a partner begins or ends; a
-- dependent child will be outside Australia; a person ceases to be a dependent child. (2): "if ... the student has dependent
-- status": becoming aware that a person has become a parent, or that another person has ceased to be a dependent child of a
-- parent. (3): "if the ABSTUDY payee is a parent": another person becomes a parent; another person ceases to be the payee's
-- dependent child. reg 19(3), (4): a parent's income exceeding the estimate by at least 25% is prescribed where the payee is
-- the student with dependent status, or the parent. reg 20(1): assets "if the student has independent status". reg 21(2):
-- "The event of the student dying is prescribed if the ABSTUDY payee is a parent of the student." Every other event in regs
-- 13, 16, 17, 18 and 21(1) is prescribed whoever the payee is.
GIVEN `payee` IS A `Who receives the ABSTUDY`
      `what` IS A `What changed`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is prescribed for this payee` IF
    CONSIDER `what`
    WHEN `someone became or stopped being the student's partner` THEN `payee` EQUALS `I am the student, with independent status`
    WHEN `a dependent child of the student will be outside Australia` THEN `payee` EQUALS `I am the student, with independent status`
    WHEN `someone stopped being a dependent child of the student` THEN `payee` EQUALS `I am the student, with independent status`
    WHEN `someone became a parent of the student` THEN (NOT (`payee` EQUALS `I am the student, with independent status`))
    WHEN `someone other than the student stopped being a dependent child of the student's parent` THEN (NOT (`payee` EQUALS `I am the student, with independent status`))
    WHEN `a parent's income for the year exceeded, or will exceed, the estimate by 25% or more` THEN (NOT (`payee` EQUALS `I am the student, with independent status`))
    WHEN `the student's (or the student and partner's) assets exceed the personal assets test limit` THEN `payee` EQUALS `I am the student, with independent status`
    WHEN `the student died` THEN `payee` EQUALS `I am a parent of the student, receiving it for the student`
    WHEN `something else` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

@export Is this change one of the events the Student Assistance Regulations prescribe for ABSTUDY (regs 12 to 21)?
GIVEN `payee` IS A `Who receives the ABSTUDY` @desc Who receives the ABSTUDY: you as a student with independent status, you as a student with dependent status, or you as a parent receiving it for the student
      `what` IS A `What changed` @desc What happened
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `Is this a prescribed ABSTUDY event` IF `it is prescribed for this payee` `payee` `what`

@export Something changed while I get ABSTUDY. Must I tell Services Australia, and by when (s 48, regs 12 to 21, 29)?
GIVEN `payee` IS A `Who receives the ABSTUDY` @desc Who receives the ABSTUDY: you as a student with independent status, you as a student with dependent status, or you as a parent receiving it for the student
      `what` IS A `What changed` @desc What happened
      `the day it happened` IS A DATE @desc The day the event happened (or, for the events about becoming aware, the day you became aware)
GIVETH A `Must I tell the Department`
`Must I report this ABSTUDY change` MEANS
    -- reg 29: the notice under s 48(1) is given by "notifying Services Australia".
    `Must I tell the Department of the event` TRUE (`it is prescribed for this payee` `payee` `what`) `the day it happened`

§§ `s 48, reg 29 -- the duty, as a rule`

DECLARE `ABSTUDY party` IS ONE OF
    `I, the ABSTUDY payee`

DECLARE `ABSTUDY act` IS ONE OF
    `notify Services Australia of the event`

-- s 48(1): "the person must notify the Department, in accordance with the regulations, of the happening of the event within 14
-- days"; reg 29: by notifying Services Australia. s 49: an offence (12 months' imprisonment) without reasonable excuse.
GIVETH A DEONTIC `ABSTUDY party` `ABSTUDY act`
`the s 48 duty` MEANS
    PARTY `I, the ABSTUDY payee`
    MUST  `notify Services Australia of the event`
    WITHIN 14
    LEST  BREACH BY `I, the ABSTUDY payee` BECAUSE "s 48(1), reg 29: a prescribed event not notified to Services Australia within 14 days (an offence under s 49 without reasonable excuse)"
